# ============================================================
# AgriGuard AI - Environment Configuration
# ============================================================
# Copy this file to .env for LOCAL development only.
# NEVER commit .env to version control!

# ============================================================
# Supabase (REQUIRED for real data)
# ============================================================
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com and create a free project
# 2. Go to Settings → API in your project dashboard
# 3. Copy your Project URL and Anon Key below
# The anon key is safe for the browser — Supabase Row Level
# Security policies protect your data, not key secrecy.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ============================================================
# AI Provider — set as a SERVER-SIDE Netlify environment
# variable instead, NOT here, and WITHOUT a VITE_ prefix.
# Anything prefixed VITE_ gets bundled into the public browser
# JS, which would leak the key. Set this in:
# Netlify dashboard → Site configuration → Environment variables
# (or via `netlify env:set GEMINI_API_KEY your-key`)
# ============================================================
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key   <- set this on Netlify, not in .env

# ============================================================
# Notes:
# ============================================================
# - With NO server-side GEMINI_API_KEY: App runs in DEMO MODE (mock data)
# - With Supabase: Real user accounts & data storage
# - With GEMINI_API_KEY set on Netlify: Real crop disease analysis
#   via the netlify/functions/analyze-crop serverless function
#
# Required tables in Supabase (see SUPABASE_SETUP.md):
# - profiles
# - farms
# - crops
# - reports
# - expert_reviews
# - notifications
